"""
SupplyShield AI – Predictive Shipment Delay Risk Intelligence

Author  : Akanksha Singh
Project : IBM SkillsBuild x AICTE Internship X BharatCares

Dataset : DataCo Smart Supply Chain for Big Data Analysis
Source  : https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shashwatwork/dataco-smart-supply-chain-for-big-data-analysis

Single-file Flask application (backend + embedded React 18 dashboard)

Runtime Design
--------------
• The application uses a frozen production XGBoost model trained on the
  DataCo Smart Supply Chain dataset.
• Due to submission size limitations, the trained model assets
  (supplyshield_frozen.pkl and processed_data.pkl) are hosted separately
  and must be placed inside the ./assets folder before running.
• On startup, the application loads the frozen model, calibrator,
  preprocessing metadata and processed dataset from ./assets.
• No retraining occurs during normal execution.
  The model used for inference is exactly the same model used during
  evaluation and reporting.
• The prediction form collects 9 business inputs.
  The trained model internally evaluates 57 engineered features.
• Categorical inputs are converted to their training-time encoded
  representations using the stored encoder metadata to ensure inference
  consistency.
• Prediction outputs include:
    - Risk Score (0–100)
    - Risk Level (Low / Medium / High)
    - Delay Probability
    - Recommended Action
• The dashboard also contains model analytics, feature importance,
  risk distribution insights and model-comparison results generated
  from the training pipeline.
"""

